# This repo is PUBLIC and cannot be made private: a GitHub Pages user site must
# be named <username>.github.io, and those are public by definition. So the rule
# here is stricter than in a normal project repo — working material stays local.
#
# The design spec and the idea capture both name private repos and local paths,
# including where personal data is kept. None of that is dangerous on its own,
# but together it maps where private data lives — published under a real name on
# the page recruiters read. Once pushed it stays in the history.
#
# Working material — commit when there is a site to explain, not before.
# Archive/ is ignored whole, not just Archive/brainstorming/: its README indexes
# what it holds, so committing the index while ignoring the contents would
# publish a description of the private material plus dead links to it.
docs/exec-plans/
Archive/

# Impeccable design-hook config: a local tooling decision, not site content.
.impeccable/
